From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Let the machine serve trapped guest accesses

The Bellatrix hook was deliberately observation-only while the address map
was being discovered.  Give the same narrow boundary a handled result now so
an optional external provider can answer a transaction without Emu68 falling
through to host memory.

Emu68 still knows no guest address ranges or device semantics.  The machine
receives the reconstructed transaction and either handles it or returns zero,
in which case the existing Emu68 path remains unchanged.
---
 src/aarch64/vectors.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/vectors.c b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
--- a/src/aarch64/vectors.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
@@ -794,7 +794,8 @@ int SYSWriteValToAddr(uint64_t value, uint64_t value2, int size, uint64_t far)
     D(kprintf("[JIT:SYS] SYSWriteValToAddr(0x%x, %d, %p)\n", value, size, far));
     
 #ifdef BELLATRIX_EMU68
-    machine_bus_access((uint32_t)far, size, 1);
+    if (machine_bus_write((uint32_t)far, size, value))
+        return 1;
 #endif
 
     if (far == 0xdeadbeef && size == 1) {
@@ -825,7 +826,8 @@ int SYSReadValFromAddr(uint64_t *value, uint64_t *value2, int size, uint64_t far)
     D(kprintf("[JIT:SYS] SYSReadValFromAddr(%d, %p)\n", size, far));
 
 #ifdef BELLATRIX_EMU68
-    machine_bus_access((uint32_t)far, size, 0);
+    if (machine_bus_read((uint32_t)far, size, value))
+        return 1;
 #endif
 
     switch(size)
